From 9f930c3b2c21ed018e64f69f37b2977c8ed126c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eileenthg <40307498+eileenthg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 00:42:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] Fix remaining compileJava errors: tag renames,
 use/useItemOn split, Tier API

- Rework CommonTags.Items references: FD's real 1.21.1 CommonTags class was
  trimmed down (verified against the real jar); missing constants now map to
  either FD's renamed FOODS_* equivalents, NeoForge's own Tags.Items
  convention tags, or the new DelightfulItemTags.SALAD_INGREDIENTS umbrella
  (across DelightfulItemTagProvider and DelightfulRecipeProvider).
- Split all block use() overrides into useItemOn()/useWithoutItem() per the
  1.21 BlockBehaviour API split (CantaloupeBlock, CantaloupePlantBlock,
  MiniMelonBlock, SalmonberryBushBlock, WildSalmonberriesBlock,
  SlicedMelonBlock, SlicedMiniMelonBlock, SlicedGourdBlock,
  SlicedGloomgourdBlock); fixed isValidBonemealTarget (dropped removed
  isClient param) and getCloneItemStack (new LevelReader/BlockPos/BlockState
  signature) across the same classes plus DPieBlock.
- Fixed DelightfulMilkshakeCauldronBlock for LayeredCauldronBlock's new
  (Precipitation, InteractionMap, Properties) constructor order and
  CauldronInteraction.newInteractionMap(String) requiring a name.
- Fixed DKnifeItem/KnifeItem constructor (attack damage/speed floats no
  longer accepted; baked into FD's real KnifeItem base class instead).
- Fixed FluixKnifeItem for the Holder<Enchantment>-based getEnchantmentLevel
  and removed Enchantments.MOB_LOOTING (now a ResourceKey-only registry).
- Removed AllthemodiumKnifeItem/AlfsteelTier's canBeDepleted()/getLevel()
  overrides (both removed from Item/Tier with no replacement).
- Fixed ForgeEvents wandering-trader offers for MerchantOffer's new ItemCost
  parameter, KnifeEvents for igniteForSeconds, ModEvents for creative-tab key
  lookup via BuiltInRegistries, DelightfulItems for BowlFoodItem's removal
  (plain Item now), RockCandyItem for Holder<MobEffect>/formatDuration's new
  tick-rate parameter, FurnaceFuelItem for getBlockEntity.
- Fixed StairBlock's now-eager BlockState constructor arg in DelightfulBlocks.

compileJava now succeeds cleanly (previously ~250 errors across 4 rounds of
this session plus earlier sessions).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
